  "notes": "USAGE:\n{押|お}しのける is an ichidan verb. It can take a direct object marked with を: {人|ひと}を{押|お}しのける (push a person aside).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}を{押|お}しのける (push people aside)\n- {周|まわ}りを{押|お}しのける (push one's way through)\n- ライバルを{押|お}しのける (beat out rivals)\n- {反対|はんたい}を{押|お}しのける (override opposition)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{押|お}しのける implies forceful removal from one's path. {押|お}し{退|の}ける is an alternate kanji spelling with the same meaning. {突|つ}き{飛|と}ばす means \"to shove away\" with more violent force.",
